Subject: [PATCH] Fill spatial reservation gaps without overtaking a sender

In the opt-in visibility profile, appending every new packet after every
conflicting future reservation makes a multicast packet block unrelated
links long before it occupies the channel. Track reservations in completion
order and admit the earliest conflict-free interval while preserving sender
FIFO and multicast exclusion. The global profile is unchanged. Release
calendar entries on delivery and client disconnect. Exercise the actual
queue with an independent gap, same-sender FIFO and a multicast barrier.

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [hwsim EasyMesh laboratory interface]

